-- where a model system stands for the human: the scope on which a reading taken in the model equals the
-- hazard in the human. Concordance is partial, so this is a scope and not an equation — 71% for rodent
-- and non-rodent together, 63% for non-rodents, 43% for rodents, and 44% for liver effects, are
-- measurements of how often an inhabitant of this type exists.
TransfersOn : BScope → (Mol → Nat) → (Mol → Nat) → Type 1
TransfersOn s a h = (M : Mol) → isTrue (s M) → a M ≡ h M
